  "query_preview": "..\nA broad trough combined with moderate upper-level divergence of the \nMarianas will continue to bring scattered thunderstorms early \ntonight. While the trough will remain, models indicate upper-level \nsupport will decrease overnight. Moisture will remain in the area\nthrough Thursday but with thunderstorm coverage will likely tapper \ndown to isolated. Scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms \nThursday will become isolated through the weekend as more stable air \nmoves into the region. Moisture will remain high enough, however, for\nisland effects showers to be possible for at least Guam over the \nnext several days. By late weekend or early next week, model guidance\nsuggests a new disturbance may develop far south-southeast of the \nMarianas, possibly bringing a new round of unsettled weather by the \nend of the forecast period.",
